1 ExplanationThe address of the structure object is reinterpreted as an int*. The first two integer members (x and y) are accessed through the converted pointer. The pointer is then reinterpreted as a char* to access the character member. Finally, the address is reinterpreted as a bool* to access the boolean member. This demonstrates how reinterpret_cast can be used to view the same memory through different pointer types.
